From f37bef42e0d334cc0425ff19f13d676eb17b01d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:25:44 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the pinned message scrolls with a scrollbar, its
 toggle shows only when needed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.32 (asks 52-54), from the operator's session on Zeo
0.11.0 (2026-11-14). Three fixes to 0102's pinned last-user-message card,
in the column 0108 keeps it to:

- Expanded, the message already scrolled past 160 px through
  overflow_y_scroll, but GPUI's overflow draws no bar, so the card read as
  cut off. The body now tracks a ScrollHandle (ThreadView's
  pinned_message_scroll) and draws Scrollbars::always_visible along it,
  the plan card's pattern. always_visible because Scrollbars::new hides
  itself when idle (the trap story 034 recorded).
- The toggle showed for every message, even a short one the minimized line
  already shows whole. It now shows only when the message has more than one
  non-blank line, or when its one line is wider than the space the header
  leaves for it; expanded, it always shows, as the way back. The width is
  known only after layout: a canvas inside the minimized body shapes the
  line with the label's own size (TextSize::Small) and records
  (entry, line width, available width) in pinned_message_fit; when that
  changes it asks for a new frame. Before the first measurement the toggle
  stays, so a long message is never left without a way to expand it. The
  rule is one pure function, needs_toggle.
- The chevron becomes the expand/collapse pair Zed ships, ExpandVertical
  ("Expand Message") and FoldVertical ("Collapse Message"), and the card
  sits on the panel's background (panel_background) instead of the lighter
  elevated surface; the border and shadow keep it apart from the entries.

Tests: pinned_message::tests gains five (a short line that fits needs no
toggle; a line wider than its space does; a second line always does; blank
lines are not a second line; an unmeasured line keeps it). Each rule was
seen failing alone: with the width comparison answering false, only the
wide-line test failed; with the line count raised to 99, only the
second-line test. Xvfb proof (debug build, a stub agent, no model):
docs/assets/zeo-6.32-pinned-card-2026-11-15/ in the hub.

§6.46 (ask 70, 2026-11-16) corrects ask 54 as this patch first read it:
the dark background belongs to an inner area around the message, as an
editor's text sits on its own surface, while the card and its border keep
the default elevated_surface_background. The icon and the toggle stay on
the card, outside the inner area.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
